Q1. Open Power BI Desktop and connect to an Excel file containing a list of your favorite restaurants (name, cuisine, rating). Load the data using the Import mode.
Ans:- Steps:
Open Power BI Desktop.
Go to Home → Get Data → Excel Workbook.
Select the Excel file containing the restaurant data.
Select the required sheet/table.
Click Load.
The data will be loaded into Power BI.
Go to Data View to check the imported data.

Import Mode:
Power BI loads a copy of the data into its model. This allows faster report performance and lets us work with the data even when the original Excel file is not currently open.

Result:
The restaurant data is successfully imported into Power BI.

Q2. Connect Power BI Desktop to a CSV file that contains IPL cricket match results (team names, scores, date). Use the DirectQuery mode and explain in one line how DirectQuery differs from Import for this data.
Ans:- Steps:
Open Power BI Desktop.
Select Home → Get Data → Text/CSV.
Select the IPL CSV file.
Preview the data.
Click Load.

Important Note About DirectQuery
A CSV file is normally loaded into Power BI using Import mode; DirectQuery is not supported for a standard CSV file in Power BI Desktop.

One-line explanation:
Import loads a copy of the data into Power BI, while DirectQuery keeps the data in the original supported source and sends queries to that source when the report is used.

If the assignment specifically requires DirectQuery:
Use a supported database such as SQL Server or MySQL for the IPL data instead of CSV, and select the DirectQuery option while connecting.

Q3. Use Power BI's Web connector to import trending movie data from a public web page (such as IMDb Top 250 or a similar site). Display the movie titles and ratings in a table visual.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the 'Get Data' > 'Web' option and enter the URL of the table page.</em>
Ans:- Steps:
Open Power BI Desktop.
Go to Home → Get Data → Web.
Enter the URL of a public webpage containing movie information.
Click OK.
Power BI will open the Navigator window.
Select the table containing movie information.
Click Load.
Go to Report View.
Select the Table visual.
Add the Movie Title and Rating fields to the table.

Result:
The table visual displays movie names and their ratings.

