Q5. Combine data from two different sources in Power BI: an Excel file with Zomato restaurant data and a CSV file with user reviews. Create a relationship between 
the tables and display the average rating per restaurant.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the 'Manage Relationships' feature to link the tables on restaurant
name or ID.</em>
Ans:- Steps:
Step 1 – Load Excel Data
Go to Home → Get Data → Excel Workbook.
Select the Zomato restaurant Excel file.
Click Load.
Step 2 – Load CSV Data
Go to Home → Get Data → Text/CSV.
Select the reviews CSV file.
Click Load.
Step 3 – Create Relationship
Go to Model View.
Find the Restaurant table and Reviews table.
Connect the common field

For example:
Restaurant[Restaurant ID] → Reviews[Restaurant ID]

If required, go to Modeling → Manage Relationships → New.
Select the two tables and matching columns.
Click OK.
Step 4 – Create Average Rating
Go to Report View.
Add a Table visual.
Add Restaurant Name from the Restaurant table.
Add Rating from the Reviews table.
Change the aggregation of Rating to Average.
